<section class="section">
  <div class="container article-body" style="max-width:920px;">
    <h2>Holiday Cookie Plate Nostalgia in a Blizzard Cup</h2>
  <p>Evoking childhood memories of holiday dough rolling and cooling wire racks, the Frosted Sugar Cookie Blizzard translates classic bakery confections into an ice-cold delight. Rather than heavy dark chocolate or nut fudges, the flavor profile hinges on delicate butter notes, sweet vanilla dough crumbles, and ribbons of silky pink confectioner's frosting. It serves as a gentle, cake-like respite on winter menu boards. Discover the complete winter and year-round rotation across <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu</a>.</p>

  <h2>Frosted Sugar Cookie vs. Confetti Cake Blizzard</h2>
  <p>Both Blizzards are in the "baked goods" flavor category. The key differences:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Frosted Sugar Cookie</strong> — Sugar cookie pieces with frosting. A more buttery, vanilla-cookie flavor. Holiday seasonal.</li>
    <li><a href="/items/confetti-cake-blizzard"><strong>Confetti Cake Blizzard</strong></a> — Cake pieces with rainbow sprinkles. More birthday-cake adjacent, brighter flavor. Summer seasonal.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Both are sweet, dessert-forward Blizzards without chocolate or peanut butter — the right choice for guests who prefer lighter flavor profiles.</p>

  <h2>Who Will Love the Frosted Sugar Cookie Blizzard?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Vanilla &amp; Buttercream Devotees:</strong> If rich cocoa or peanut butter feels overpowering, this creation shines a spotlight on pure vanilla bakery extracts and sweet cream.</li>
    <li><strong>Festive Family Gatherings:</strong> Its cheerful pastel sprinkles and buttery profile make it an instant hit with children celebrating winter school breaks.</li>
    <li><strong>Balanced Calorie Count:</strong> At approximately 510 calories for a Small, it provides satisfying seasonal decadence without crossing into the 800+ calorie range of extreme chocolate fudges.</li>
  </ul>

